{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Me and my [G]uncle went ridin' [Em]down
South Color-ado, [G]West Texas [Em]bound
We stopped [G]over in Santa [Em]Fe
That point [G]being just [G#]about half [A]way
And [G]you know it was the [B7]hottest part of the [Em]day[Em]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I took the horses up to the stall
Went to the barroom, ordered drinks for all
Three days in the saddle, you know my body hurt
It bein' summer, I took off my shirt
And I tried to wash off some of that dusty dirt
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
West Texas cowboys, they's all around
With weed, liquor and money, they're loaded down
So soon after payday, you know it seemed such a shame
You know my uncle, he started a friendly game
Of High-low jack and the winner takes the hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
My uncle starts winnin' – them cowboys got sore
One of them called him out lord then two more
‘Accused him of cheatin' - oh lord, it couldn't be
I know my uncle and he's as honest as me
And I'm as honest as a Denver man can be
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
One of them cowboys, he starts to draw
I shot him down, Lord, he never saw
Shot me another, he won't grow old
And in the confusion my uncle he grabbed their gold
And we high-tailed it down to Mexico
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
I love those cowboys, I love their gold
I loved my uncle, God rest his soul
He taught me good, Lord, taught me all I know
Taught me so damn well, I up grabbed that gold
And I left his dead-ass there by the side of the road
And I left his dead-ass there by the side of the road
(retard..haha) And I left his dead-ass there by the side of the road
{end_of_verse}
